# below, never reproduced. Quoting them here made this file itself trip the
# repository's Credential and Artifact Audit ("Generic secret assignment
# detected"), which was the scanner behaving correctly: a high-entropy
# assignment in a newly committed file is exactly what it exists to catch.
# SECURITY.md offers a `scanner:allow-secret <reason>` pragma, but also warns
# that several pragmas in one file means the values do not belong there. They
# do not. Read the cited line in security.yml to see the actual fixture.

